<title>USA: Dotronix sees lower Q2 sales.</title>
<headline>Dotronix sees lower Q2 sales.</headline>
<dateline>NEW BRIGHTON, Minn. 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dotronix Inc said on Thursday that it expects continued weaker sales through the fiscal second quarter.</p>
<p>Earlier, it reported a drop in sales for the first quarter ended September 30 to $3.0 million from $4.0 million a year ago.</p>
<p>The company said revenue declined because of a decrease in shipments for a Federal Aviation Administration upgrade program in the first quarter.</p>
<p>In the second quarter ended December 31, 1995, Dotronix's sales were $3.1 million.</p>
<p>Dotronix designs and makes high resolution video displays.</p>
<p>Reuters Chicago Newsdesk - 312-408-8787</p>
